[{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"eaa478dd44c3dac8d3a951af1bd2cf302b47ba67a0c712140a68d89d7e9f8dd7","event_uuid":"f340f3d9-fe95-412e-8872-e35b6afa6c31","position":{"commit_sha":"40f3ee5582e293160fb76c69bb68963e2d7cacf2","position":"1788469009682412127-f340f3d9-fe95-412e-8872-e35b6afa6c31"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"d2d9abd556283ffef3490944c825ad96a478c66c424ee1e5424cf42c4cc42467","event_uuid":"dccd3b69-401f-4209-a4fd-62f2619bc138","position":{"commit_sha":"4c0fa6c300b6e350d5d03da900e00945889c5402","position":"1788469062672205239-dccd3b69-401f-4209-a4fd-62f2619bc138"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e6d0a86796e40b33f321e36d92edd2bcc8a7b515abba5908f604908ef691e383","event_uuid":"78f1d50c-5100-4b4b-96a0-b5e7225d8564","position":{"commit_sha":"c1ec1a1c6588220fe8101796e5f4e5323e813f2a","position":"1788469271058774532-78f1d50c-5100-4b4b-96a0-b5e7225d8564"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Calibration sample frozen before review.\n\nPopulation: 610 non-archived/visible work tickets of type bug, epic, story, or task whose description length is 7,200–7,999 characters (near) or >=8,000 (over). Excluded session_log and code_review. Selection seed: `20260903-bloat-v1`; rank within each type×band stratum by SHA-256(seed + \":\" + canonical ticket id), then take fixed quotas. Quotas yield 20 unique tickets: five per type and ten per band. This is deterministic preliminary calibration, not prevalence estimation.\n\nShared in all three batches:\n- cibophobic-moist-guineafowl (b928-3ab6-5985-417b), bug, near, 7,855\n- uncheered-sombre-bumblebee (f789-3f9d-8b35-4e0d), story, over, 12,128\n\nBatch A unique:\n- exultant-neofascist-bluegill (1e88-687f-45d1-435f), bug, near, 7,322\n- outrageous-uncultured-wildebeast (0e68-41eb-5782-4336), epic, near, 7,707\n- amenable-befuddling-phoenix (2e0f-e4dc-ee9d-4855), story, near, 7,916\n- coyish-fluent-gibbon (e7a9-35fa-1d58-4095), bug, over, 8,801\n- dissimilar-sorcerous-hartebeest (3393-83ca-5501-4e6e), epic, over, 11,165\n- punctual-scavenger-fallowdeer (2682-b015-4fe5-4066), task, over, 8,379\n\nBatch B unique:\n- camerashy-erectable-frog (301d-0769-ed02-42f6), bug, near, 7,446\n- spin-cub-usher (65dd-e93b-666a-4caa), epic, near, 7,976\n- synonymous-senatorial-cuscus (6e2f-2814-4f92-4873), task, near, 7,965\n- strained-bare-turnstone (df2c-e4b8-496d-4698), bug, over, 10,536\n- elfish-chair-lug (88ab-7052-8850-46d4), epic, over, 18,787\n- enduring-cagophilic-orca (1de3-a19f-c4ea-4b28), story, over, 8,135\n\nBatch C unique:\n- picky-censorable-loon (69e3-748d-0274-45f3), story, near, 7,580\n- sepia-cardiac-hawk (ddcd-fc9e-a81f-4cbb), story, near, 7,243\n- blousy-luxuriant-rasbora (ce7d-3a15-51e5-4c6a), task, near, 7,947\n- jira-reb-1003, epic, over, 10,892\n- stew-kid-motif (6a9a-910a-6938-4695), task, over, 10,393\n- lofty-beech-twang (a118-fa8e-547a-49ba), task, over, 17,211\n\nReviewers will see frozen rule definitions and complete ticket material, but not computed detector firings. They will label overall bloat and each rule's targeted construct as present/absent/not-applicable with evidence and confidence.","timestamp":1788469271058774532}],"created_at":1788468460796481096,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"eb75fefc-79ec-4c78-a3ce-5158e38cf717","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"ee0c-1d25-1652-43c3"},{"link_uuid":"dccd3b69-401f-4209-a4fd-62f2619bc138","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nCalibrate the preservation-first verbosity guidance and ten deterministic bloat rules from immobile-drastic-springtail against historical rebar tickets whose descriptions are near or above the 8,000-character admission limit. Save the prior research as a session_log and add session_log to the artifact contract.\n\n## Approach\n- Build a read-only population of work tickets (task, story, bug, epic) with description length 7,200–7,999 or at least 8,000 characters. Exclude session_log and code_review artifacts from the sampled population because their intentionally verbose semantics would confound the work-ticket policy.\n- Freeze the ten proposed rules and compute whether each rule fires on the applicable description/comment content. Use normalized Markdown comparisons while protecting identifiers, paths, commands, dates, measurements, decisions, constraints, blockers, and exact errors.\n- Split a reproducible sample into at least three small batches of 6–8 tickets. Background reviewers receive complete rule definitions but not the computed firing results. Each labels overall appropriateness/bloat and, per applicable rule, whether that rule’s targeted bloat is actually present, with concise evidence and confidence.\n- Aggregate per-rule TP, FP, FN, and TN counts and percentages over applicable artifacts. Also report union-of-rules performance for overall ticket bloat, not-applicable counts, sample composition, disagreements/uncertainty, and threshold changes suggested by observed false positives/negatives.\n- Treat the exercise as a preliminary calibration, not population-level validation; state sample-size and selection-bias limits.\n\n## Artifacts\n- A rebar session_log containing the prior research, source links, guidance, deterministic rule matrix, and this calibration’s progress/results.\n- Ticket comments containing the sampling method, batch assignments, measurements, and final confusion matrices.\n- No repository files.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The prior research is saved in a linked session_log, and session_log is added to the artifact contract as the home for verbose chronology/evidence.\n- [ ] At least three background-agent batches of 6–8 near/over-limit work tickets are reviewed.\n- [ ] Every sampled ticket has a reproducible identifier, description length, length band, overall bloat label, confidence, and concise rationale.\n- [ ] For each applicable rule, TP/FP/FN/TN counts, denominators, and percentages are reported; not-applicable cases are separate.\n- [ ] Overall union-of-rules performance and material reviewer uncertainty are reported.\n- [ ] Recommendations distinguish observed evidence from provisional threshold changes and identify false-positive safeguards.\n- [ ] No repository files are modified.\n\n## Verification\nCross-check batch outputs against the frozen sample, recompute confusion matrices deterministically, verify the session_log link, and record results on this ticket.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Read-only ticket-history calibration; findings and evidence live in rebar ticket comments and a linked session_log.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"8631d44f-028a-4342-93cd-25c881bad96c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":["rebar"],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["research","agents","writing-quality","calibration"],"ticket_id":"ee2e-6fec-aa8a-4e77","ticket_type":"task","title":"Calibrate verbosity rules against long ticket history","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f258992c-5d86-41e2-9c6b-0234b8942a5b","eb75fefc-79ec-4c78-a3ce-5158e38cf717","4b22b83a-c7ef-458a-9f4d-5310af1b21de","8bd452e7-ac67-4d34-a7de-ccaa2b2ea2aa","8631d44f-028a-4342-93cd-25c881bad96c","f340f3d9-fe95-412e-8872-e35b6afa6c31","dccd3b69-401f-4209-a4fd-62f2619bc138","78f1d50c-5100-4b4b-96a0-b5e7225d8564"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788469271058774533,"uuid":"5b2493df-2ae0-4cd2-b3b1-6d2e8ec6f5be"}